When wearing gauntlets/boots of fumbling, you have a chance to hit
yourself when you try to apply your pickaxe.  Also when you stumble you
stop running.  I haven't seen any other negative effects.

What I'd like is for fumble-armour to be more dangerous -- you might
fall on top of a cockatrice corpse, randomly step in the wrong
direction, drop your weapon, bump into friendly monsters... as it is,
the armour is only a minor annoyance until you uncurse it or destroy it.

